at your option.

Why both: MIT is the licence most implementers already have cleared internally, and
Apache-2.0 carries an express patent grant that MIT does not. A specification is
implemented by many independent parties who thereby step into the same patent claims,
so the grant matters here in a way it does not for ordinary application code. Taking
either licence is sufficient; nobody has to take both.

